<%# The frame every email this app sends goes through.

    Deliberately old-fashioned: one presentation TABLE at most 600px wide,
    a system font stack and no remote images at all. The wordmark is TEXT —
    an image would be blocked by half the mail clients on earth, would leak
    an "opened" signal to whoever hosted it, and would break the day a CDN
    hiccups. Widths and colours are written inline as well as in the style
    block, because Outlook ignores most of the block and Gmail drops it in
    some views.

    The BODY is left alone. Signer mail carries wording the customer wrote
    (SubmitterMailer's custom bodies, rendered from Markdown), so the layout
    puts a frame around it and imposes nothing inside it — no headings, no
    accent colours, no restyled links.

    Three signatures sit at the bottom, and each answers a different question.

    The SUPPORT line is on platform notices and nowhere else — billing,
    account, quota, invitations, operator, SMTP, the mail we write to the
    person who runs an account. It is deliberately absent from signer mail
    even on a free account: a signer's questions are about the DOCUMENT, and
    they go to the person who sent it, not to us. Putting our address at the
    bottom of somebody else's correspondence only misdirects them.

    The WORDMARK is the platform's too, but it answers "who runs this?", which
    a signer does have a reason to ask. So it stays on signer mail and
    disappears only when that account has paid for branding removal — and it
    stays on a platform notice whatever the flag says, because the reader has
    to recognise who is writing to them.

    The line underneath comes from shared/mailer_attribution, and it is NOT
    the DocuSeal attribution — a previous version of this comment said it was
    and was simply wrong. The AGPL attribution points are the interactive ones
    (shared/_powered_by, shared/_attribution), which `rake gates:branding`
    pins. What the partial carries in mail is the product's own "Sent using
    EsignCenter…" line, which an account may switch off once it has paid for
    branding removal — and, on a platform notice, the plainer "Sent by
    EsignCenter" instead, because a bill reminder is not the place to sell
    free document signing. %>
<% content = yield %>
<% notice = platform_notice? %>
<% branded = notice || !Accounts.branding_removed?(@current_account) %>
<%# Rendered up here so the footer rule below can ask whether it said anything.
    The partial decides for itself whether the "Sent using" line appears; all
    this does is avoid drawing an empty bordered strip under a mail where it
    decided not to and there is no support line either. Nothing here can
    suppress it — `attribution` is printed verbatim whenever it has content. %>
<% attribution = render(partial: 'shared/mailer_attribution') %>
<% footer = notice || attribution.to_s.strip.present? %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title></title>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <style>
      body { margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100% !important; background-color: #f4f5f7; }
      table { border-collapse: collapse; }
      .ec-body { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #1f2933; }
      .ec-body p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
      .ec-body ul, .ec-body ol { margin: 0 0 16px; padding-inline-start: 22px; }
      .ec-body li { margin: 0 0 6px; }
      .ec-body h1, .ec-body h2, .ec-body h3 { margin: 0 0 12px; line-height: 1.3; }
      .ec-body a { color: #1d4ed8; }
      .ec-foot { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: #6b7280; }
      .ec-foot p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
      .ec-foot a { color: #6b7280; }
      @media only screen and (max-width: 620px) {
        .ec-pad { padding: 24px 20px !important; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body dir="<%= TextUtils.rtl?(content) ? 'rtl' : 'auto' %>" style="margin: 0; padding: 0; background-color: #f4f5f7;">
    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color: #f4f5f7;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding: 24px 12px;">
          <table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width: 100%; max-width: 600px; background-color: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px;">
            <% if branded %>
              <tr>
                <td class="ec-pad" style="padding: 24px 32px 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">
                  <div data-mail-wordmark style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.2px; color: #111827;"><%= Docuseal.product_name %></div>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
            <tr>
              <td class="ec-body ec-pad" style="padding: <%= branded ? '20px' : '32px' %> 32px 32px; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #1f2933;">
                <%= content %>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <% if footer %>
              <tr>
                <td class="ec-foot ec-pad" style="padding: 20px 32px 24px; border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: #6b7280;">
                  <% if notice %>
                    <p data-mail-support style="margin: 0 0 8px;"><%= mail_to Docuseal::SUPPORT_EMAIL %></p>
                  <% end %>
                  <%= attribution %>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
